{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5140-1","published":"2026-11-09T13:24:47Z","modified":"2026-11-10T13:15:07.782924083Z","related":["CVE-2026-102700","CVE-2026-102703","CVE-2026-102704","CVE-2026-62437","CVE-2026-79602","CVE-2026-79603","CVE-2026-79609","CVE-2026-79610","CVE-2026-79611"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-102700","CVE-2026-102703","CVE-2026-102704","CVE-2026-62437","CVE-2026-79602","CVE-2026-79603","CVE-2026-79609","CVE-2026-79610","CVE-2026-79611"],"summary":"Security update for xen","details":"This update for xen fixes the following issues:\n\nSecurity issues fixed:\n\n- CVE-2026-62437: x86: DMs may cause mem leak by IRQ binding (bsc#1276838).\n- CVE-2026-79602: x86: improper handling of HVM emulation return codes (bsc#1276839).\n- CVE-2026-79603: unconditionally do TLB flushing ahead of page scrubbing (bsc#1276841).\n- CVE-2026-79609: x86: XPTI may break on huge-memory systems (bsc#1283321).\n- CVE-2026-79610: grant-table: double version change race (bsc#1283322).\n- CVE-2026-79611: VMX: VMentry failure with branch tracing and blocked states (bsc#1283323).\n- CVE-2026-102700: gnttab: cache-flush handling may cause page reference leak (bsc#1283325).\n- CVE-2026-102703,CVE-2026-102704: arbitrary read/write via grant copy (bsc#1288663).\n\nNon security issue fixed:\n\n- Update to Xen 4.18.6 security bug fix release (bsc#1027519).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"xen","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server 15 SP6-LTSS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/xen&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%2015%20SP6-LTSS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.18.6_03-150600.3.56.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"xen":"4.18.6_03-150600.3.56.1","xen-devel":"4.18.6_03-150600.3.56.1","xen-libs":"4.18.6_03-150600.3.56.1","xen-tools":"4.18.6_03-150600.3.56.1","xen-tools-domU":"4.18.6_03-150600.3.56.1","xen-tools-xendomains-wait-disk":"4.18.6_03-150600.3.56.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/secur